# What is uploaded to Vercel.
#
# Vercel reads this file INSTEAD of .gitignore when it exists, so the exclusions
# that matter are restated here explicitly rather than inherited. The rule is
# simple: a file that must never leave this machine is named in this file.
#
# `.env` holds DATABASE_URL (with the database password), JWT_SECRET (the cookie
# signing key) and the storage credentials. It is here on the first line of the
# list for that reason — not as a trailing detail.

# --- Secrets. Never uploaded. ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Local state ---
.local-storage/
# The dev server's build directory. Distinct from .next because `pnpm dev` writes
# to .next-dev; uploading it would ship a half-built dev bundle to the builder.
.next-dev/
.manus-logs/

# --- The pre-PostgreSQL data ---
# Restated here rather than inherited from .gitignore, because Vercel reads THIS
# file *instead of* .gitignore. Both files are gitignored and both would otherwise
# be uploaded on every deployment, and they are the most sensitive thing in the
# project: the MySQL export carries 781 accounts with scrypt password hashes,
# teacher names, and the text of disciplinary matters. It is the only copy of the
# pre-migration data, which is exactly why it belongs in a backup and not in a
# build upload.
#
#   database/tsc_case_management_dump.sql   the MySQL source, hand-exported
#   database/postgres-load.sql              generated by pnpm db:convert
#
# Named individually, not as database/*.sql, so bootstrap.sql and test-data.sql
# stay in the upload — they are source, and neither holds real data.
database/tsc_case_management_dump.sql
database/postgres-load.sql

# --- Build output and dependencies. The builder produces its own. ---
.next/
node_modules/

# --- Local tooling and logs ---
*.log
.dev.vars
.turbo/
coverage/

# --- Documentation sources kept in the repo but not needed to build ---
# tsc-doc.pdf is the manual the platform implements, kept for provenance.
